# "When another creature you control leaves the battlefield, transform Aang at the beginning of the next upkeep." On turn 3
# Bot1 exiles its own Ornithopter with Swords to Plowshares: it leaves the battlefield without dying, and the delayed ability
# waits. It does nothing during the rest of Bot1's turn; it triggers at the next upkeep, which is Bot2's on turn 4, "regardless
# of whose turn it is" (the 2025-10-02 ruling), and Aang becomes Aang, Destined Savior, a 4/4 flier. Bot2's combat on turn 4 is
# not "combat on your turn" for Bot1, so nothing is earthbent then. At the beginning of combat on Bot1's turn 5 Aang earthbends
# 2: the Forest becomes a 0/0 land creature with haste and two +1/+1 counters, and as a land creature Bot1 controls it has
# vigilance, so it attacks beside Aang and stays untapped while Aang, no land, taps.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Aang, at the Crossroads
Ornithopter
Swords to Plowshares
Island x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x16

[Actions]
